 Ayotte (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Governor Kelly Ayotte enters the final weeks of her reelection race against Democrat Cinde Warmington as a clear favorite. Every pollster to survey the race since late summer has shown Ayotte ahead, with high-quality surveys from Saint Anselm, UNH, YouGov, and Siena putting her lead between four and eleven points. Aggregated averages place the margin near ten points, and prediction markets give Warmington roughly a one-in-twenty chance.\n\nNew Hampshire's slight Democratic lean and an Obama endorsement in late October give Warmington theoretical openings, and the candidates have clashed over taxes, school funding, marijuana, and affordability in recent debates. But none of the available evidence shows the race moving: expert ratings cluster at Likely R, and Ayotte's lead has been stable across more than a dozen polls spanning six months.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -8.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0566, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0654, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0698, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0784, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1135, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0954, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0873, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0914, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1036, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0759, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0785, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0513, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -8.5}, {